From 3845b8df125cb85ae1570d06fd1f9a0fb3a106f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:04:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs: fix four more claims the code contradicts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- AGENTS.md said tsconfig runs `strict: false` and a .tsx file gets no type
  checking. The same tree sets `strict: true` and includes src/**/*.tsx, so a
  .tsx file is checked, strictly. `checkJs: false` (the JS half) was correct
  and is kept. Still don't add TypeScript to src/ — but for the convention
  reason, not a false one about the compiler.
- rollback.md used `git revert -m 1 <sha>`. We squash-merge, so a merged PR is
  a one-parent commit and -m fails on it — the emergency rollback could not
  run. Branch on the parent count.
- verify.md Step 1 ran `git checkout master`, which git refuses when the
  primary worktree already holds master — i.e. every time /verify runs from a
  feature worktree. Locate the worktree that has master and work there.
- verify.md Step 2 took "the most recently merged PR". If anything merged in
  between, cleanup would remove the wrong worktree and branch and close
  unrelated issues. Verify the PR by number, resolved from HEAD if not given.

Found by codex review on PR #132.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
